	skos:definition "A wireless network connection facet is a grouping of characteristics unique to a connection (completed or attempted) across an IEEE 802.11 standards-conformant digital network (a group of two or more computer systems linked together). [based on https://www.webopedia.com/TERM/N/network.html]" ;
